    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a favorable slate today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who remains our premier start with an 81.88 efficiency score. Despite a 33% rain risk in his matchup against Keider Montero, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an optimal #3 spot and a strong platoon advantage against the right-hander. Following closely is **Luis Robert Jr.** (75.66), who leverages a significant platoon boost against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez to project as our most potent outfield option. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** earns a surprise surge to 73.61; while his #8 order placement creates a slight drag, he is capitalizing on a high-ceiling matchup against Max Scherzer, whose 5.89 xERA makes him a primary target for our middle infield efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Curtis Mead** (53.86) out of the starting nine. While **Curtis Mead** carries a favorable park factor and a platoon edge against Jack Perkins, the optimizer favored the specific situational upside of **Drake Baldwin** and **Jacob Wilson**, both of whom are projected for better volume due to their projected lead-off roles. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with **Sam Antonacci** and **Dominic Smith**, both of whom hover near the 40\u201350 range; their scores are suppressed by challenging matchups against Max Fried and Zac Thornton, respectively. We are closely monitoring the status of **Heliot Ramos**, whose 58.25 score is buoyed by favorable winds, though he faces a slight efficiency dip due to the opposing catcher's elite ability to control the run game\u2014a critical factor given our strategy of prioritizing stolen base efficiency.",
